{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And the Medanites sold him to Egypt.</b> Measure for measure: through the tribes Joseph was sold to become a slave in Egypt, and they [the Medanites] were there as slaves; afterward they and their children settled there generation after generation, and they learned from the ways of the Egyptians, until the Egyptians became jealous of them and enslaved them and afflicted them." "<b>To Egypt.</b> In Egypt, as in ״ואל הארון תתן את העדות״ (and into the ark you shall place the testimony), ״מים חיים אל כלי״ (living waters into a vessel), אל תוך שרפת הפרה (into the burning of the cow)." "<b>Officer of the butchers.</b> As its Targum: רב קטוליא — the officer appointed by the king over those liable to death, to execute them by the judgment decreed upon them. For we find the concept of killing in the language of slaughtering, as it is written: ״לטבוח ישרי דרך״ (to slaughter the upright of way)."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:49.802051320Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}